{"name":"Lebanon Cedar","hex":"#3c341f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cedar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A coniferous tree of the genus Cedrus in the family Pinaceae.","A coniferous tree of the family Cupressaceae, especially of the genera Juniperus, Cupressus, Calocedrus, or Thuja."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cedar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cedrus libani","blocks":[{"text":"Cedrus libani, commonly known as cedar of Lebanon, Lebanon cedar, or Lebanese cedar, is a species of large conifer in the pine family, Pinaceae, and is native to the mountains of the Eastern Mediterranean basin. Known for its longevity, height, and durable wood, it has held profound significance for millennia. The tree features in ancient Mesopotamian literature. It is the national emblem of Lebanon and is widely used as an ornamental tree in parks and gardens. Historically, the ancient Phoenicians used Cedar wood for shipbuilding and traded Cedar trees with Ancient Egypt, Ancient Greece, Anatolians, Iberians, Punics, Sicilians, Romans and Ancient Iraq."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/C%C3%A8dre_du_Liban_Barouk_2005.jpg/330px-C%C3%A8dre_du_Liban_Barouk_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedrus_libani","wikidata":"Q61105"},{"title":"Lebanon","blocks":[{"text":"Lebanon, officially the Lebanese Republic, is a country in the Levant region of West Asia. Situated at the crossroads of the Mediterranean Basin and the Arabian Peninsula, it is bordered by Syria to the north and east, Israel to the south, and the Mediterranean Sea to the west; Cyprus lies a short distance from the coastline. Lebanon has a population of more than five million and an area of 10,452 square kilometres (4,036 sq mi). Beirut is the country's capital and largest city."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Flag_of_Lebanon.svg/330px-Flag_of_Lebanon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lebanon","wikidata":"Q822"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Cedrus_libani_shoot.jpg/500px-Cedrus_libani_shoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Cedrus_libani_shoot.jpg/1280px-Cedrus_libani_shoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Cedrus_libani_shoot.jpg/500px-Cedrus_libani_shoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Foliage","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACedrus_libani_shoot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Cedar_of_Lebanon_cone.JPG/500px-Cedar_of_Lebanon_cone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Cedar_of_Lebanon_cone.JPG/1280px-Cedar_of_Lebanon_cone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Cedar_of_Lebanon_cone.JPG/500px-Cedar_of_Lebanon_cone.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Female cone showing flecks of resin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACedar_of_Lebanon_cone.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Male_cone_of_Cedar_of_Lebanon.JPG/500px-Male_cone_of_Cedar_of_Lebanon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Male_cone_of_Cedar_of_Lebanon.JPG/1280px-Male_cone_of_Cedar_of_Lebanon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki